<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Our standards for original comparisons, factual accuracy, safety boundaries, updates, and corrections.">
  <h2>Original, purpose-led coverage</h2>
  <p>Every article must answer a specific reader question and add a distinct comparison, checklist, workflow, or decision framework. We do not publish bulk pages that merely swap product names or repeat the same article.</p>
  <h2>Primary sources and clear attribution</h2>
  <p>Where a claim depends on a policy, specification, safety framework, or product statement, we prefer the responsible organization’s own documentation. Sources are listed near the relevant guide so readers and search systems can verify the basis of the article.</p>
  <h2>Safety boundaries</h2>
  <p>We do not provide instructions for synthetic undressing, non-consensual intimate imagery, identity abuse, or evasion of platform safeguards. Safer alternatives remain fully clothed and require informed adult consent.</p>
  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>Each guide displays publication and update dates. Material corrections should change the updated date and, where helpful, explain the revised conclusion. Requests for factual correction can be submitted through the Contact page.</p>
  <h2>AI-assisted workflow</h2>
  <p>AI tools may assist with research organization, drafting, code, or visual ideation. Final pages are reviewed for usefulness, consistency, safety, sourcing, and duplication before publication.</p>
</InfoPage>
